34,2,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The station block is still fighting over a broken latch. Their minutes show they can’t even agree on sweeping. We need a system that doesn’t rely on goodwill.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, that’s sad. The complaint log shows one household filed eleven of fourteen complaints. That’s not just annoyance; that’s resentment.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Shizue, resentment is a symptom of unfairness. The measurements show the narrowest frontage is only ninety centimetres. That’s a trap for maintenance.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, ninety centimetres is tiny! And the truck comes at seven forty. That’s before I wake up. If we move it, will the smell just follow us?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, the smell follows open bags. The ledger shows we spend thirty-four thousand yen a year on nets and deodorant. We are paying for the problem.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, paying for the problem is bad. But the residents' meeting showed nobody wants to be the enforcer. We need a structure that makes cooperation easy.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, exactly. If we can’t talk without fighting, the new location is just a new place to resent each other. I want a place that feels peaceful.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shizue, peace requires clarity. The filing requirements say a permanent build needs four months and five signatures. That’s a lot of hours just in paperwork.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, four months is forever! I want to know if the new spot will smell bad in summer. I don’t want to wake up to a stinky surprise.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, the subsidy covers forty percent, capped at ninety thousand. Last year’s shelters averaged two hundred forty-eight thousand. We need to know the true cost.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, the cost is high. But the real cost is the silence. If we pick a plan that forces us to interact constantly, we’ll hate each other.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, I agree. But if we don’t sleep together, we lose them entirely. I want a place where we can still be neighbours, not just strangers.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shizue, neighbours require boundaries. Option A locks the burden on one household. Option B rotates the load. Option C keeps it static but controlled.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, Option B sounds like a big adventure for the bins! But if the bins move, the smell moves too! I don’t want that.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, Option B is exhausting. Option A is predictable. But we must ensure the new location doesn’t replicate that unequal burden.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I’m leaning towards Option C. It keeps us apart, which is safer. We don’t need to be friends, just functional.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Kenji, distance isn’t the answer. Option B spreads the hours fairly, so nobody burns out. I’m voting B.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Shizue, Option B is a trap. It forces constant interaction. Option C distributes the load fairly. I am voting C.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I like Option B! Moving it around means nobody gets stuck with the smell forever. It’s like a big adventure for the bins!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, Option B is too tiring. Option A is the most predictable and least exhausting for our budgets. I’m voting A.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
